+# HAOS WebUI Compatibility Audit
+
+Date: 2026-09-22
+Branch: `haos-compat-verification-20260922`
+Repository: `/media/DADOS_1TB/Projetos/HAOS-WEBUI`
+
+## Result
+
+No production-code fix was applied. The verified WebUI behavior is compatible with the
+current standalone Python WebUI service when it is launched with the HAOS Agent virtual
+environment. The audit found deployment/integration blockers that require explicit
+HAOS wiring rather than a safe local code change.
+
+## Prioritized findings
+
+### P0 — HAOS port/topology contract is not implemented by this repository
+
+Evidence:
+
+- `api/config.py` defines the WebUI service default as `127.0.0.1:8787`.
+- A repository-wide Python search found no `8786` reference and no upstream proxy
+  route to a separate Python backend.
+- SSE and API routes are handled locally by `api/routes.py` (`/api/chat/stream`,
+  `/api/sessions/events`, and related routes).
+
+Impact: if HAOS expects this WebUI to be a client/front end for the HAOS Python
+backend on `127.0.0.1:8786`, that topology is not supported by the current WebUI.
+The WebUI must either remain the service bound on `:8787` or receive a separately
+designed adapter/proxy contract. I did not invent that contract or modify the
+production service.
+
+### P1 — Reverse-proxy forwarded-host trust is opt-in and exact
+
+Evidence:
+
+- CSRF/origin validation compares the browser origin with `Host` by default.
+- `X-Forwarded-Host` and `X-Real-Host` are considered only when
+  `HERMES_WEBUI_TRUST_FORWARDED_HOST` is truthy.
+- Explicit cross-origin access requires exact scheme/host/port entries in
+  `HERMES_WEBUI_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`; malformed entries are ignored.
+- `tests/test_cors_preflight_allowlist.py` verifies no wildcard CORS and exact
+  allowlisting; the targeted suite passed.
+
+Impact: an HAOS edge/proxy deployment must set the forwarded-host trust flag and,
+when the browser origin differs from the upstream Host, configure the exact allowed
+origin. Enabling forwarded headers without a trusted proxy boundary would weaken
+origin checks, so no default was changed.
+
+### P1 — Runtime is source-coupled to Hermes Agent modules
+
+Evidence:
+
+- `scripts/audit_agent_source_dependencies.py` reports 7 dependency classes and
+  248 findings, including direct imports of `hermes_cli.*`, `agent.*`, `hermes_state`,
+  and `hermes_constants`.
+- With `HERMES_WEBUI_AGENT_DIR=/usr/local/lib/haos-agent` and the HAOS Agent venv,
+  `api.config._AGENT_DIR` resolved to `/usr/local/lib/haos-agent` and
+  `run_agent.__file__` resolved to `/usr/local/lib/haos-agent/run_agent.py`.
+- Importing the same runtime with the WebUI-created `.venv` failed because that
+  environment lacks the Agent's `requests` dependency. The supported launcher path
+  selects the Agent venv; direct launches must follow the documented requirement.
+
+Impact: an HAOS deployment must preserve the Agent source/module boundary and use
+the Agent venv (or install the complete compatible dependency set). A standalone
+WebUI container without the Agent source/dependencies is not currently compatible.
+
+### P2 — SSE headers are proxy-aware, but end-to-end proxy delivery was not verified
+
+Evidence:
+
+- Stream handlers emit `text/event-stream`, `Cache-Control: no-cache`, and
+  `X-Accel-Buffering: no`.
+- Several legacy/short-lived streams emit `Connection: close`; long-lived paths
+  explicitly omit it where required by the source comments.
+- Unit coverage includes `tests/test_approval_sse.py`; the targeted suite passed.
+- No live HAOS edge process was restarted or modified, so delivery through the
+  optional Rust edge on `:8787` is unverified.
+
+Impact: verify buffering, idle timeouts, disconnect propagation, and auth-cookie
+forwarding through the actual HAOS edge before production rollout.
+
+## Verification evidence
+
+- `python3 -m compileall -q server.py bootstrap.py api`: passed.
+- `node --check static/*.js`: passed for every static JavaScript file.
+- `./scripts/test.sh --collect-only -q`: 16,074 tests collected.
+- Focused integration/runtime slice: 248 passed in 28.68s.
+- Isolated server smoke with temporary `HERMES_HOME`, temporary
+  `HERMES_WEBUI_STATE_DIR`, port `18987`, and HAOS Agent directory:
+  `/health` returned HTTP 200 with a JSON health payload; process exited 0 after
+  termination.
+- Full `./scripts/test.sh -q`: started 16,074 tests but was terminated after the
+  tool's bounded wait window while still running; it showed failures before
+  termination. Those failures were not diagnosed and are not claimed as a full-suite
+  pass.
+
+## Files changed
+
+- This report only: `docs/haos-compatibility-audit-20260922.md`
+- No production source, service unit, HAOS runtime state, or HERMES-TURBO file was
+  modified.
